{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790460725,"nonce":"uwwIBEA5hJC8WXpgcr/noMZbttk=","title":"Python: InlineHint::Always on comparators, small dunders and dispatcher arms (P-comparator-inline-hint)","message":"Part C of P-error-flag-attrs, not done in that package. The compiler side is in place: an `inline_always` annotation on a TypedFunction lowers to InlineHint::Always (and always_inline), and the HIR dump shows `; attrs: inline_always`. The inliner does not honour the hint yet (C-inliner-budgets owns that), so setting it today changes nothing measurable.\n\nOwed in crates/zyntax_python:\n1. comparator and key functions a sort/sorted/min/max site passes, when they are typed closures or module functions;\n2. small operator dunders: no loop, no call to a non-dunder program function, a single return or at most three simple statements (Vec3.__add__, GVector.__mul__);\n3. the arm calls of a generated dispatcher with at most five arms (richards' Task$fn overrides at `t.fn(pkt)`), as a per-call hint if HIR gets one, else on the override.\n\nMeasure with ZYNTAX_TRACE_INLINE skipped-reasons on richards, crypto_pyaes and raytrace once C-inliner-budgets lands; drop any hint class that pushes a caller over the post-inline budget.","files":null}]}